#ASSERT `s 15K(2): the failure to lodge an explanatory statement affects the validity or enforceability of the instrument` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 15L: notice of events (text lines 427 to 446)`

#ASSERT `s 15L: the responsible person must give notice to the First Parliamentary Counsel of the event` TRUE `an event resulting in, or otherwise affecting, the commencement of the Act or instrument (or a provision of it)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 15L: the responsible person must give notice to the First Parliamentary Counsel of the event` TRUE `the occurrence of a day or time specified in the Act or instrument, or the making of a commencement instrument, resulting in or affecting commencement` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 15L: the responsible person must give notice to the First Parliamentary Counsel of the event` TRUE `a discretionary compilation event` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 15L: the responsible person must give notice to the First Parliamentary Counsel of the event` TRUE `a required compilation event` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 15L: the responsible person must give notice to the First Parliamentary Counsel of the event` TRUE `an event resulting in the Act or instrument (or a provision of it) being repealed, lapsing, expiring or otherwise ceasing to be in force` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 15L: the responsible person must give notice to the First Parliamentary Counsel of the event` TRUE `an event resulting in the Act or instrument, or a provision of it, being (or being declared by a court or tribunal to be) invalid or unenforceable` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 15L: the responsible person must give notice to the First Parliamentary Counsel of the event` TRUE `the responsible person's becoming aware of an error in the Register to which subsection 15D(1) may apply` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 15L: the responsible person must give notice to the First Parliamentary Counsel of the event` TRUE `the responsible person's becoming aware of any other error in the Register` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 15L: the responsible person must give notice to the First Parliamentary Counsel of the event` TRUE `another event prescribed by the rules for the purposes of paragraph (1)(f)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 15L: the responsible person must give notice to the First Parliamentary Counsel of the event` TRUE `for a disallowable legislative instrument, the disallowance of the instrument or a provision of it` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 15L: the responsible person must give notice to the First Parliamentary Counsel of the event` TRUE `for a disallowable legislative instrument, the disallowance of another legislative instrument (or a provision of one) that amends the instrument` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 15L: the responsible person must give notice to the First Parliamentary Counsel of the event` TRUE `the amendment or repeal of a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument by the operation of Part 3 of Chapter 3` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 15L: the responsible person must give notice to the First Parliamentary Counsel of the event` TRUE `the amendment or repeal of a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument by the operation of Part 4 of Chapter 3` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 15L: the responsible person must give notice to the First Parliamentary Counsel of the event` TRUE `another event prescribed by the rules for the purposes of paragraph (2)(e)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 15L: the responsible person must give notice to the First Parliamentary Counsel of the event` TRUE `any other event` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 15L: the responsible person must give notice to the First Parliamentary Counsel of the event` FALSE `an event resulting in, or otherwise affecting, the commencement of the Act or instrument (or a provision of it)` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 15L: the responsible person must give notice to the First Parliamentary Counsel of the event` FALSE `the occurrence of a day or time specified in the Act or instrument, or the making of a commencement instrument, resulting in or affecting commencement` EQUALS NOTHING
